\pard\ql\f0\fs30\sa180 \b 1 Operating principles\b0 \par
\pard\ql\f0\fs22\sa180 1.1 Preserve the existing all-layer execution path as the fast path. The degenerate all-active configuration must not perform sampling, construct active-index lists, or add per-layer membership tests.\par
\pard\ql\f0\fs22\sa180 1.2 Keep N_LAYERS as the canonical architectural and depth-basis length. Selected layers retain their nominal indices.\par
\pard\ql\f0\fs22\sa180 1.3 Implement selection outside compact materialisation. Dense and compact models should consume the same logical-layer selection mechanism.\par
\pard\ql\f0\fs22\sa180 1.4 A sampled selection is fixed for an optimizer update and all of its gradient-accumulation microsteps. Resampling cadence is expressed in completed optimizer updates.\par
\pard\ql\f0\fs22\sa180 1.5 Evaluation and generation always execute all N_LAYERS layers in v1.\par
\pard\ql\f0\fs22\sa180 1.6 Preserve existing code paths and THOG source-marking conventions.\par
\page
\pard\ql\f0\fs30\sa180 \b 2 Stage 1 - layer dropout\b0 \par
\pard\ql\f0\fs26\sa180 \b 2.1 Configuration\b0 \par
\pard\ql\f0\fs22\sa180 Add the following run/training controls:\par
\pard\ql\f2\fs19\sa100 layer_dropout_stratum_size\par
\pard\ql\f2\fs19\sa100 layer_dropout_active_per_stratum\par
\pard\ql\f2\fs19\sa140 layer_dropout_resample_steps\par
\pard\ql\f0\fs22\sa180 Defaults shall resolve to all layers active. Validate N_LAYERS % stratum_size == 0, 1 <= active_per_stratum <= stratum_size, and resample_steps >= 1.\par
\pard\ql\f0\fs26\sa180 \b 2.2 Sampler\b0 \par
\pard\ql\f0\fs22\sa180 Add a small deterministic sampler utility. Each contiguous stratum begins at layer 0 boundaries and contributes exactly active_per_stratum uniformly sampled distinct nominal indices. Sort the union before execution.\par
\pard\ql\f0\fs22\sa180 Selection identity shall be derived from model_seed and resample bucket so DDP ranks and resumed runs reproduce the same active set without checkpointing sampler state.\par
\pard\ql\f0\fs26\sa180 \b 2.3 Trainer lifecycle\b0 \par
\pard\ql\f0\fs22\sa180 Resolve the active set once at the start of each optimizer update, before the gradient-accumulation loop. Reuse it for every microstep. A resample bucket spans layer_dropout_resample_steps completed optimizer updates.\par
\pard\ql\f0\fs26\sa180 \b 2.4 Logical-layer execution\b0 \par
\pard\ql\f0\fs22\sa180 Extend the shared logical-layer executor to accept an optional ordered sequence of nominal layer indices. When no sequence is supplied, execute the existing range(N_LAYERS) path unchanged.\par
\pard\ql\f0\fs22\sa180 Activation-checkpoint segments shall be formed over consecutive active execution positions while _logical_block continues receiving the original nominal layer index.\par
\pard\ql\f0\fs26\sa180 \b 2.5 Model interface\b0 \par
\pard\ql\f0\fs22\sa180 TrainingDenseGPT and TrainingSheetGPT shall expose the selected layer sequence to the shared executor. The all-active state shall be represented so that forward calls take the unchanged fast path.\par
\pard\ql\f0\fs26\sa180 \b 2.6 CLI, identity, and telemetry\b0 \par
\pard\ql\f0\fs22\sa180 Expose long-form CLI controls through run_thog2_owt.py and train_OWT.sh. Record resolved controls and derived active-layer count in run configuration/checkpoint identity and avoid run-name collisions. Do not print full selected-index lists on normal progress lines.\par
\page
\pard\ql\f0\fs30\sa180 \b 3 Test and release gates\b0 \par
\pard\ql\f0\fs22\sa180 3.1 Unit-test validation, exact per-stratum cardinality, no duplicates, deterministic resampling, resample cadence, and sorted nominal indices.\par
\pard\ql\f0\fs22\sa180 3.2 Regression-test the all-active path against current execution, including a guard proving the sampler is not invoked.\par
\pard\ql\f0\fs22\sa180 3.3 Test that the selected set is constant across gradient-accumulation microsteps and changes only on configured resample boundaries.\par
\pard\ql\f0\fs22\sa180 3.4 Test activation checkpointing with sparse nominal indices and confirm _logical_block receives original indices.\par
\pard\ql\f0\fs22\sa180 3.5 Test evaluation uses all layers regardless of the training selection.\par
\pard\ql\f0\fs22\sa180 3.6 Test dense and compact models, resume determinism, configuration identity, and CLI plumbing.\par
\pard\ql\f0\fs22\sa180 3.7 Run the CPU unit-test suite locally before the branch is presented as complete.\par
\page
\pard\ql\f0\fs30\sa180 \b 4 Explicit deferrals\b0 \par
\pard\ql\f0\fs22\sa180 4.1 No non-uniform probability distributions.\par
\pard\ql\f0\fs22\sa180 4.2 No forced endpoint retention.\par
\pard\ql\f0\fs22\sa180 4.3 No fractional/non-integer depth coordinates.\par
\pard\ql\f0\fs22\sa180 4.4 No uneven strata or automatic remainder allocation.\par
\pard\ql\f0\fs22\sa180 4.5 No inference-time stochastic layer selection.\par
